# std/run-async (design/caos-expr.md): an entry for an OPERATION OF THE STEP. `@op` says llm-step
# does the work in process (it owns the conversation's own records and the call's
# lifecycle), so this entry exists to give the operation a path, a help and a place in
# `tool_help`/`run_tool`. The image it curries is never run.
HELP=<<END
Start or inspect an already-constructed CAOS request in the background. The request must be a complete 40-character ArgTree hash already stored in CAOS. Repeating the same request reads the same durable task; once complete, the result includes its result hash. Use this only for independent work whose complete context is in the request: detached work does not inherit secrets, credentials, model settings, or other ambient execution context.
@param request The complete CAOS request (ArgTree) hash to run independently.
@op run-async
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-step --help=$HELP
